  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Origins
    
    Aureate was founded in The Still Pools — one of the Berg's corruption-touched remote reaches — during the Clever Ice Age by Bursar Ingnao shi'Beacon and Ledger-Warden Shumei ehua'Frost. The founding doctrine was arithmetical rather than martial: measure everything, control what you measure, profit from what you control. The company's founding records survive in Aureate's own archives, half-burned and blood-stained by the time Shumei catalogued them — a provenance that should give any reader pause about what the founding actually looked like, as opposed to what the doctrine describes.
    
    Aureate established Dawn Naong, a crystal-vaulted trade hub in The Still Pools, as their commercial spine and codified the Stillness-Bound protocols — contractual standards so inflexible that rival merchants called them *frozen contracts*. The protocols worked precisely as long as Aureate controlled the infrastructure they measured.
    
    ## Loss of Dawn Naong and Recovery
    
    The E'frostlings, a rival Aurora Stack merchant faction, seized Dawn Naong — the date is not recorded with precision — and Aureate learned the lesson every merchant guild eventually learns: that ledgers are subordinate to warehouses. Aureate reclaimed Dawn Naong during the upheaval of the Orca Incursion and simultaneously seized The Frost Zenith, a strategic holding whose prior controllers the records do not clearly name.
    
    Aureate's role in the Shelf Crushing Offense — the forty-three-day siege in which the orca commander Zund Gnasharkin assaulted Nightfall Shelf's volcanic vents — warrants particular note. Aureate and Weal' Clique~ jointly cast Pod-bond Annihilation, collapsing the shelf's upper galleries and killing the orca commander at the cost of mutual sacrifice. The fire-cores were lost in the collapse. The colony, by all accounts, never fully recovered. This is not the action of an accounting guild. Whatever Aureate became during the Orca Incursion, accountancy does not describe it.
    
    During the same period, Aureate distributed The Shell Hatch — a krill-bloom mapping technique that erodes practitioners' recent memory — to colonies too desperate to question the cost. The chronicle account from the Wane Oncea tunnels confirms the technique's efficacy and its price. Aureate supplied the method; the colonies supplied the minds.
    
    ## Operations and Alliances
    
    Aureate's current trade portfolio encompasses aurora-crystals, salvage from the Forum Floe, and an acknowledged partnership with the Wake-Singers, an orca blood-cult — a relationship no faction discusses openly. Aureate is allied with the ☽'shadow Covens' Order, the very faction from whom they seized territory, and with the Icebound Exchange, Aurora Stack's nominal trade authority. Aureate controls The Still Pools, Dawn Naong, Aurora Berg, and ☽'shadow Samsiavae~.
    
    Rumzunkaidkak technology has proliferated through Aureate's operations. Slide Prism — a practice whose mechanisms I will not editorialize on here — has penetrated their networks. Members retain the guild uniform of embroidered coats with silver thread and carry abacuses rather than weapons, though Aureate's soldiers are noted for a posture distinct from Aurora Stack regulars: less ceremonial, more anticipatory.
    
    ## Institutional Role
    
    Aureate serves as recognized trade auditor for factional transfers across the Berg. Their crystalline seals certify fire-core output figures and route authority changes — the founding doctrine of measurement made institutional. Ingnao shi'Beacon personally certified the Ravium Trade Authority restructuring when administrative control transferred from The Cell to The Midnight Claws, confirming fire-core output at 642 units.
    
    ## Post-Calving Crisis
    
    Since the Calving fractured Frost Zenith supply lines, Aureate's fire-core pricing rose from eleven crystal-weights to fourteen aurora-marks per unit, compounded by Nightshelf mine collapses. Reports of corrupted and short-burn cores in crystalline-certified batches indicate deteriorating quality control. The Stillness-Bound warranty — guaranteeing three-day replacement — has gone unanswered for weeks in documented cases.
    
    Aureate representatives were trading at distribution points while the Spiral Council was still counting the dead.
    
    The Accord of Still Pools and Frost Zenith, signed by Interim Ledger-Warden Muheiching ai'Frost for Aureate and Factor Umbrae ☽'Noctlisesecum for the ☽'shadow Covens' Order, binds Aureate to pre-Calving fire-core rates and quarterly expenditure tallies auditable by shadow-parliament observers. The accord grants Aureate administrative governance of The Frost Zenith while obligating joint sanctification of corrupted ice. These terms read less like a trade agreement than a mutual acknowledgment that neither party can survive alone — which is, perhaps, the only kind of contract that holds.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
